  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Among the following the number of curves not in accordance with Freundlich adsorption isotherm is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2e7c5e7b-f7ea-443a-a38b-098a5dad0ce2-image.png\" style=\"width: 193px; height: 150px;\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ab4d4f15-c52d-43f6-970a-e2a8ef98527b-image.png\" style=\"width: 193px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/962a7018-f129-48eb-afbd-88f3c56a694c-image.png\" style=\"width: 197px; height: 150px;\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1f05683b-c861-4909-a4a1-c19eb99d80a2-image.png\" style=\"width: 202px; height: 150px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Freundlich, in 1909, gave an empirical relationship between the quantity of gas adsorbed by unit mass of solid adsorbent and pressure at a particular temperature. The relationship can be expressed by the following equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>KP</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>Where x is the mass of the gas adsorbed on mass m of the adsorbent at pressure P, k and n are constants which depend on the nature of the adsorbent and the gas at a particular temperature. The relationship is generally represented in the form of a curve where mass of the gas adsorbed per gram of the adsorbent is plotted against pressure.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mi>logp</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>logk</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/19955060-2d70-489c-92ba-810167c915d6-image.png\" style=\"width: 193px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p>Freundlich isotherm explains the behaviour of adsorption in an approximate manner. The factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math> can have values between 0 and 1</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
